# Waterfall Model

## Introduction
The Waterfall Model is a software development model where each phase is completed before moving to the next phase.

## Phases
1. Requirement Analysis
2. System Design
3. Implementation
4. Testing
5. Deployment
6. Maintenance

## Real-World Example
A college library management system can be developed using the Waterfall Model when its requirements are clearly defined.

## Advantages
- Simple to understand
- Easy to manage
- Suitable for projects with fixed requirements

## Disadvantages
- Difficult to accommodate changes
- Testing happens after implementation

## Conclusion
The Waterfall Model is suitable for projects where requirements are well understood and unlikely to change.
